nucleo src/boxcar.rs: 32-bit PowerPC has no 64-bit atomics, so std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64 does not exist there
("Unable to resolve `use` target std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64", helix 25.07.1; rustc on ppc32 fails the same way).
The lock-free vector's `inflight` push counter is a u64 on purpose: indices are u32, and a u64 can't wrap, so `push`
catches running past them (`try_into().expect("overflowed maximum capacity")`). A plain AtomicU32 would wrap to an
index in use. On targets without 64-bit atomics the counter is an AtomicU32 that a compare-exchange loop never
increments past u32::MAX; once there, it reports u32::MAX + 1 and `push` panics as before. 64-bit targets keep the
AtomicU64. The call sites are unchanged (`load` still returns u64). Same code in every release 0.0.0..0.5.0 (the
`push` hunk has no leading context: its signature changed in 0.5.0).

--- a/src/boxcar.rs
+++ b/src/boxcar.rs
@@ -26,3 +26,7 @@
